course: dictionary
lesson: 5537
title: Words that last: legacy
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A legacy is something that stays behind after a person or event is gone. The words around it give you clues. «The Romans left a legacy of straight roads across Britain.» Roads still stand long after the Romans have gone, so legacy means something left from the past.
explain: Legacy can also mean money or property left to someone in a will when a person has died. Context tells you which meaning you need. If the sentence is about a grandmother's savings or house, think money or property. If it is about ideas, buildings or history, think what remains.
explain: The phrases «leave a legacy» and «a lasting legacy» both point to something that lasts. To check your meaning, swap in "something left behind". If the sentence still makes sense, you have probably understood the word.
fact: A legacy is money or property left to someone by a person who has died.
fact: A legacy can also be something that stays after a person or event is gone, such as their ideas or buildings: «his legacy».
fact: «The legacy of the Romans» means the things they left behind, such as roads and buildings.
fact: In computing, a «legacy system» is old technology still in use. It means old, outdated software.
fact: Legacy is a noun, and its plural is legacies.
exercise: «The Romans left a legacy of straight roads across Britain.» What does legacy mean here? | A kind of weather | *Something left behind from the past | A new computer game | Money left in a will
exercise: «Grandma's legacy paid for our new house.» What does legacy mean here? | A school test | Something the dog left in the garden | *Money left to someone when a person has died | A type of bridge
exercise: In computing, what is a «legacy system»? | A brand new game | *An old system still in use | A fast new phone | A type of keyboard
test: «The scientist's ideas were her lasting legacy.» What does lasting legacy mean? | A broken toy | A short holiday | *Something good that stays after she is gone | A quick snack
test: Which word is the plural of legacy? | legaci | *legacies | legacyes | legacys
exam: «Ahmed left a legacy of kindness.» What does legacy most likely mean here? | *Something good that stays after he is gone | A type of sport | A map of the town | A bill to pay
